#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:5
msgid "7. Splitting up: Routers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:7
msgid "So far everything lives in one file. That works until your bot has 30 handlers — then you want modules. :class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.router.Router` splits a bot into independent, mountable pieces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:13
msgid "Creating a router"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:15
msgid "A ``Router`` is created, filled with handlers, and then included into the dispatcher:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:51
msgid "Handlers registered on the router behave exactly as if they were registered on the dispatcher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:56
msgid "Multiple routers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:58
msgid "Include as many as you like — order defines priority:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:68
msgid "An update flows through the routers in order; the first handler whose filters match wins, and propagation stops there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:73
msgid "Nesting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:75
msgid "Routers can contain routers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:85
msgid "This lets big projects mirror their package structure in the bot layout. Deeply nested routers are cheap — propagation just walks the tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:91
msgid "Naming routers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:93
msgid "``Router(name=\"notes\")`` makes logs readable: when an update is handled, the dispatcher logs which router it ended up in. For debugging unfamiliar codebases, name your routers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:99
msgid "Startup and shutdown hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:101
msgid "Every router has its own ``startup`` and ``shutdown`` observers, fired recursively by the dispatcher:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:115
msgid "Use them to open and close database connections owned by the module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:119
msgid "Recap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/07_router.rst:121
msgid "You can now split a bot into ``Router`` modules, mount them in priority order, nest them, and give each module its own lifecycle hooks. Next: intercepting every update with middlewares."
msgstr ""
